The comment on this line assumes a batch-wide error means the actor's coach data is globally unavailable. It doesn't. services/coaches/relationships/coachee.go:71-99 shows `ManyCoachedBy` doesn't batch at the datastore layer, it fans out one `getCoachCoacheePair` per kaid in a tracegroup and `err := g.Wait()` returns the first error. `acl.ManyCoachedByActorErr` then discards every successful result (`return result, err` with `result` still the empty map, pkg/khan/acl/coaches.go:114-116); this loader copies that one error into all `len(kaids)` slots; and `isActorCoachOrAdminBatched` (acls.go:120-131) logs it, gets `coached=false` for all, and falls through to `actorIsProgressViewingAdminForUser`, which a plain teacher fails.

